# gdlint configuration for gladiator-engine.
#
# Only the keys below are overridden; every other rule keeps gdtoolkit's
# default, so this file does not freeze the rest of the ruleset in place.
#
# max-file-lines stays at gdtoolkit's default of 1000, deliberately.
#
# The repo this configuration came from ran at 1200, raised from the default
# when one class crossed 1000 and then repeatedly landed back on the new
# ceiling -- five tasks in five days, each one ending in an extraction done
# purely to fit, and at one point a task with nowhere to put a three-line
# member. That project inherited the problem; this one starts with no legacy
# debt and no reason to buy runway it has not spent.
#
# The rule that history teaches: when a file approaches the limit, split it.
# Raising the number trades a bounded refactor for a few more tasks of
# runway and puts the same failure on someone else's pull request. Note that
# max-file-lines cannot be auto-fixed, so it goes straight to red and waits
# for a human -- which is the point.
max-file-lines: 1000
